Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0028 (touches attention.py only).
EXL3_ROWMM=1 (default off; needs the vllm_exl3_moe plugin): V4.1's decode-size bf16 attention-input projections run on
the plugin's row GEMM (vllm_exl3_moe/rowmm.py, csrc/exl3_router.cu rowmm) instead of cuBLAS: the compressor's fused
wkv / wgate [1024 | 512, 5120] -> fp32 (kv-source layers 2, 8, 14, 20), the indexer's weights_proj [32, 5120] -> bf16
(the 8 index layers) and wk [128, 512] -> bf16 on the compressor latent. On GB10 cuBLAS takes 87-97 us for the
compressor's 10.5 MB (split-K, ~108 GB/s) and 40-55 us for weights_proj's 0.33 MB; both run on aux streams beside
wq_a + wkv (31-42 us) and the default stream joins them before wq_b, so index layers ran ~47 us and kv-source layers
~105 us longer than plain layers, ~0.6 ms a round (prose profile, Oct 21). The row
GEMM streams one weight row a warp at DRAM rate for up to 8 rows; any other shape (prefill, larger batches), a missing
plugin or the flag off keeps today's path. fp32 sums in a fixed order: deterministic, not bit-equal to cuBLAS's split-K
order, so a rounding-class change (bf16 outputs rounded to nearest even as F.linear's). Tests: plugin
tests/test_rowmm_gpu.py (rowmm vs fp64, bf16 = rounded fp32, ok() refusals, CUDA-graph replay).

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py
